.policy "typescript-eslint-no-unsafe-declaration-merging" revision 2
.description "Don't give a TypeScript class and an interface the same name in one scope; the merge adds the interface's members to the class without checking them."
.language typescript
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

#include "tsx/ts-b-scope.rr"
//   variable

// typescript-eslint's no-unsafe-declaration-merging: `interface A { x: number } class A {}` merges the two, and the
// class then claims an `x` it never sets. Both names are reported.
//   interface A {} class A {}   declare class B {} interface B {}                → each name reported
//   namespace N { export interface C {} } class C {}   interface D {} namespace D {}    fine
// One quirk is kept: the rule looks an interface's name up from the interface's own scope, which, for an interface
// with type parameters, is the scope of those parameters, where the name is not; so `interface E<T> {}` beside
// `class E<T> {}` reports only the class. No options.
.violation no_unsafe_declaration_merging(at: node) code "@typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-declaration-merging" "Rename the class or the interface so they don't merge; merged, the class claims the interface's members without implementing them."
    suppress eslint "@typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-declaration-merging"
    suppress biome "lint/suspicious/noUnsafeDeclarationMerging"
no_unsafe_declaration_merging(id) :- variable(s, x, id, "class"), variable(s, x, _, "interface").
no_unsafe_declaration_merging(id) :- variable(s, x, id, "interface"), variable(s, x, _, "class"), field(i, "name", id),
    !field(i, "type_parameters", _).
